          "text": "is distinct from deployment. It does **not** deploy a Glue compute job, Airflow service, identity-backed approval API, or a complete AWS lakehouse. AWS execution needs a selected account/region, scoped identity, spending limit, workload, failure/retry logs, and teardown evidence. No `apply` is run by CI. ## Limits and roadmap The graph is a deterministic tool workflow, not a learned planner benchmark. Approval is an explicit local-operator decision bound to the proposal hash; the in-memory checkpoint is lost on restart, and local process owners are trusted. It is not an authenticated multi-user approval service. Driver collection and full-table comparison are bounded to this historical dataset. Do not infer distributed throughput or production adoption. Next: durable approval identity/checkpoint storage, independent-source fault labels and seasonal drift calibration, then a separately approved AWS integration. First-release CI passed for the local integration, actual Airflow execution, Terraform validation and full-history scanner. AWS deployment remains pending. See [CHANGELOG](CHANGELOG.md)."
